Text latex:
  Relative chains are defined as the cokernel of the singular-chain map induced
  by the inclusion of the relative subset into the ambient subset.
  Relative homology is the homology of this complex in the selected degree.
  These constructions do not yet supply the relative maps, connecting morphisms,
  excision, or the well-group theorem.

Result chain cokernel kills its defining map:
  Attribution: topology; CategoryTheory.Limits.cokernel.condition; adapted
  Let K: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let C,D: ModuleChainComplex(K,field)
  Let f: ChainMap(K,field,C,D)
  Conclude:
    compose chain maps(field,C,D,chain cokernel(field,C,D,f),
      chain cokernel projection(field,C,D,f),f) =
        zero chain map(field,C,chain cokernel(field,C,D,f))

Result singular chain homology agrees:
  Attribution: topology; AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor; direct
  Let K: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let H: HomologyTheory(K,field)
  Let X: TopologicalSpace
  Conclude: chain homology(field,singular chains(field,H,X),H.degree) = homology module(field,H,X)

Result relative chains are the inclusion cokernel:
  Attribution: topology; relative singular chain definition; original
  Let K: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let H: HomologyTheory(K,field)
  Let X: TopologicalSpace
  Let Q: TopologicalPair(X)
  Conclude:
    relative chains(field,H,X,Q) =
      chain cokernel(field,singular chains(field,H,subspace(X,Q.relative)),
        singular chains(field,H,subspace(X,Q.ambient)),pair chain inclusion(field,H,X,Q))

Result relative homology uses the selected degree:
  Attribution: topology; relative singular homology definition; original
  Let K: Type
  Let field: FieldStructure(K)
  Let H: HomologyTheory(K,field)
  Let X: TopologicalSpace
  Let Q: TopologicalPair(X)
  Conclude: relative homology(field,H,X,Q) = chain homology(field,relative chains(field,H,X,Q),H.degree)

